                  and map building},
  booktitle =    {{ICRA}},
  year =         2001,
  volume =       4,
  pages =        {4238--4243},
  abstract =     {This paper analyzes the properties of the full covariance
                  simultaneous map building problem (SLAM). We prove that, even
                  for the special case of a stationary vehicle (with no process
                  noise) which uses a range-bearing sensor and has non-zero
                  angular uncertainty, the full-covariance SLAM algorithm always
                  yields an inconsistent map. We also show, through simulations,
                  that these conclusions appear to extend to a moving vehicle
                  with process noise. However, these inconsistencies only become
                  apparent after several hundred beacon updates.},
}

