                  where the negotiation is taking place between different agent,
                  negotiating about different tasks. After the allocation each
                  of the robots gets it's subtask and develops it's own plan,
                  there is a problem in oreder not to get conflicting plans in
                  terms of accomplishing subtask and using resources. While each
                  robot executes it's plan the failure may occur and the the
                  planner is reinitiated. There is a lot of planning going on
                  which may be quite time consuming also robots are assigned
                  priorities in the allocation phase. Is a good idea?
                  Negotiation is going on only on the symbolic level and is to
